From: Alex Lennon <ajlennon@dynamicdevices.co.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: st1010: use continuous DSI clock

The ST1010 panel now completes its HX8279-D command initialization, but the
physical panel remains uniformly pale while DRM scans a verified checkerboard
from an active 1200x1920 XR24 framebuffer.  This isolates the remaining fault
to the DSI video link rather than the framebuffer, LCDIF, panel power, or DCS
command path.

Unlike the BOE panels whose descriptor this integration started from, the
ST1010 specification gives a continuous 468 MHz MIPI clock and 980 Mbps lane
rate and does not specify non-continuous clock operation.  Keep its clock lane
in HS while video is active so the dual HX8279-D receivers retain byte-clock
lock across blanking intervals.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-himax8279d.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-himax8279d.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-himax8279d.c
@@ -1151,7 +1151,7 @@ static const struct panel_desc santek_st1010_hx8279d_panel_desc = {
 	.width_mm = 229,
 	.height_mm = 143,
 	.mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO | MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_SYNC_PULSE |
-			MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS | MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM,
+			MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM,
 	.format = MIPI_DSI_FMT_RGB888,
 	.lanes = 4,
 	.on_cmds = santek_st1010_hx8279d_on_cmds,
-- 
